ID: B2-Ch01a-Intro
TEXT:

"Our first objectives?" Hadrik's jaw drops as he stares up at the sky. "Did that little runt actually say objectives?"

"That is correct, you heard me!" The projection of Golmyck, king of Thilias, bellows from the glowing screens suspended over the rooftops, as though answering the dwarf directly. "I am about to announce the trial for the tournament's opening round. Pay close attention. I have no intention of repeating myself. Are you ready?"

The gnome waits a beat, smoothing the lapels of his rumpled coat.

"Splendid!" he continues. "Your task is straightforward. Each participant must secure a glowing pinecone and deliver it to the city of Galamir. These specimens grow exclusively on Varathia, so outsiders may find them unfamiliar. In appearance, they resemble ordinary pinecones in every respect—until you take them in your hand, at which point they ignite with bright light. There is no time limit for this trial. However, those who deliver their pinecone earliest will receive their next objective immediately, securing a substantial head start over late arrivals. Finally, alliances are permitted. A team may contain as many members as you please. If every member confirms the alliance upon reaching Galamir, the entire group advances together—provided you present at least one glowing pinecone between you. That concludes the briefing. Good luck to all!"

"What?!" Hadrik's voice echoes off the brick walls. "Is this a joke? A mage tournament, and we're sent foraging in the brush? What next, a bouquet-weaving contest?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Intro2-dead, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Intro2-dead, v_checkpoint_rich = 0) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Intro2-alive, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Intro2-alive, v_checkpoint_rich = 0) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 1)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Intro2-dead
TEXT:

"Hadrik..." Daren's voice is low, his jaw set in a hard line. "I could not care less about the tournament right now."

"Ah, before I forget—one urgent administrative matter!" Golmyck's voice booms across the square before the feed can cut. "Daren, the healer in plate armor, along with every member of his retinue, must report to the gates of the royal castle of Thilias in precisely five hours. That includes the dwarf, the artificial mage, and the lessathi. Failure to appear will result in immediate disqualification. The young girl in their company is welcome to attend, though her presence is not mandatory. Thank you for your cooperation, and have a pleasant afternoon!"

The gnome jabs a switch on his console. The transmission cuts with a sharp crackle, and the holographic displays flicker, dissolving into thin blue mist over the alleys.

"Hold on," Hadrik says, scratching his beard. "How does he know Barry is a lessathi? Barry barely figured that out himself."

"The king knowing about Barry and Kate means we have been watched from the moment we crossed the gates," Illuna says through Flower's lips, her tone icy and clipped. "His informants report every movement in this city. It would not surprise me in the least if he knows I am here as well."

"Great," Hadrik mutters, shoulders sagging. "If his spies are that thorough, he probably knows I'm a giant. They're dragging us to the castle to throw me out on my ear."

"They are summoning us over the dead noble," Daren says, scanning the empty street. "There are bounties on our heads. An interrogation was inevitable. We need to reach Rose's estate. The clinic is out of reach without her to navigate these alleys, and we cannot face the king without our gear."

Daren stops, his chest rising in a heavy breath.

"And one of us," he says, staring at the flagstones, "has to tell her brother and sister that she is dead."

choice("Volunteer to deliver the news to the kids", B2-Ch01a-Volunteer, v_ac_b2_ch1_news = 1, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Volunteer, v_b2_ch1_volunteer = 1)
choice("Stay silent", B2-Ch01a-Silent, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Silent, v_b2_ch1_volunteer = 0)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Intro2-alive
TEXT:

"Perhaps tracking them requires a spell?" Rose offers gently. "I have studied local flora for years, and glowing pinecones have never appeared in any of my texts."

"Ah, before I forget—one urgent administrative matter!" Golmyck's voice booms across the square before the feed can cut. "Daren, the healer in plate armor, along with every member of his retinue, must report to the gates of the royal castle of Thilias in precisely five hours. That includes the dwarf, the artificial mage, and the lessathi. Failure to appear will result in immediate disqualification. The young girl in their company is welcome to attend, though her presence is not mandatory. Thank you for your cooperation, and have a pleasant afternoon!"

The gnome jabs a switch on his console. The transmission cuts with a sharp crackle, and the holographic displays flicker, dissolving into thin blue mist over the alleys.

"Hold on," Hadrik says, scratching his beard. "How does he know Barry is a lessathi? Barry barely figured that out himself."

"The king knowing about Barry and Kate means we have been watched from the moment we crossed the gates," Illuna says through Flower's lips, her tone icy and clipped. "His informants report every movement in this city. It would not surprise me in the least if he knows I am here as well."

"Great," Hadrik mutters, shoulders sagging. "If his spies are that thorough, he probably knows I'm a giant. They're dragging us to the castle to throw me out on my ear."

"They are summoning us over the incident with the noble," Daren says. "There are bounties on our heads. An interrogation was inevitable. Come on, we need to hurry to the clinic. Time is short."

"The clinic can wait," Rose says, placing a hand on his forearm. "None of the wounded are in critical danger, and you have only five hours to reach the royal gates. We have to retrieve your packs from my estate first, and walking from there to the castle takes nearly two hours on foot."

"Does this city have no carriages for hire?" Daren asks. "Something to make better time?"

"Like what?" Rose asks, puzzled.

"Well... horse-drawn cabs? Carts?"

"Gods above, no!" Rose draws back, horrified. "Enslave a horse to drag a wagon? That is as cruel as the hunts! Besides, the beasts fled the city decades ago when the hunting started. They live under the golden fox's protection now."

"Right, right," Daren rubs the back of his neck, grimacing. "The animals speak here. My mistake. Let us move, then. Maintain a steady march and we will make the deadline."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Spin, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Spin)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Volunteer
TEXT:

achievement("Bearer of bad news",v_ac_b2_ch1_news)
"I'll do it," I say. "I'll try to break it to them as gently as possible."

Daren studies me, his brow furrowed. Leaving such news to me clearly sits uneasy with him, but the relief in his posture is unmistakable. Nobody else steps forward; Kate stares at the dirt, and Flower wrings the hem of her shirt.

"Very well," Daren says quietly. "Barry will speak to the children. Any objections?"

Silence hangs over the alley. Kate keeps her gaze fixed on the stones.

"Let us move," Daren says, turning on his heel. "We retrace our steps so we do not lose our bearings. Stay close."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Spin, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Spin)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Silent
TEXT:

I keep my mouth shut, and the silence stretches across the cobblestones. Kate and Flower stare at the dirt, refusing to look up. Hadrik shifts his weight from boot to boot, rubbing the back of his neck with a thick palm.

"I will speak to them," Daren says when no one answers. "Move out. We have no time to waste. Retrace our path so we do not lose our bearings. Stay close."

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Spin, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Spin)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Spin
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
"Can I have Arraka back, please?" Flower asks Hadrik as we turn down the alley toward the estate.

"I think I'll hold on to her a little longer, if you don't mind," Hadrik says with a wide grin.

"Well... all right," Flower says. "Just don't drop her."

"Not a chance," Hadrik says, winding the chain around his thick index finger. "I'm giving her my undivided personal attention."

We fall in behind Daren, tracing our path out of the cramped, leaning tenements of the lower ward into the paved avenues of the upper district.

Not a soul speaks. Even Hadrik's usual chatter dies out. Kate takes it worst of all—she walks with her head bowed, staring at her boots, her jaw clenched tight enough to crack bone. Through the grim silence, Arraka's voice shrills from the golden amulet, spewing curses, threats of flaying, and promises of eternal torment as Hadrik swings the chain in lazy, rhythmic loops.

"Shut her up, Hadrik," Daren snaps, without turning around. "I have had enough of Arraka's voice to last three lifetimes. I will not listen to her screech the entire march."

"Right, right," Hadrik mutters. He clicks the casing shut and resumes twirling it by the chain.

The banshee's muffled shrieks drift up from the spinning gold, reduced to a dull, buzzing rattle.

"My wrist is going numb," Hadrik says after a few minutes, shaking out his forearm. "Barry, want a turn? I swear to you, it's remarkably therapeutic."

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
