choice(""Sure, why not?"", B2-Ch01a-Sure-dead, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Sure-dead, v_b2_ch1_spin = 1) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
choice(""I think I'll pass, thanks."", B2-Ch01a-Pass-dead, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Pass-dead, v_b2_ch1_spin = 0) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 0)
choice(""Sure, why not?"", B2-Ch01a-Sure-alive, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Sure-alive, v_b2_ch1_spin = 1) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 1)
choice(""I think I'll pass, thanks."", B2-Ch01a-Pass-alive, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Pass-alive, v_b2_ch1_spin = 0) if (v_ch11_saved_rose == 1)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Sure-dead
TEXT:

"Sure, why not?" I say, catching the chain as Hadrik tosses it over.

I start looping the amulet around my wrist. Arraka's muffled screeches rise in pitch, though through the sealed casing the words blur into furious buzzing. I am almost certainly better off not deciphering them.

"I've been thinking," Kate says, breaking the heavy quiet. "Is it possible Rose isn't entirely gone? Could some part of her still be trapped inside that body?"

"Kate..." Daren begins, his tone weary, but she talks over him, her voice tightening.

"There might be a way to pull her back!" She looks between us, searching our faces for any shred of agreement. "If we hunt down that servant of Ulruk who took her, we might reverse it. We can't know for certain until we try."

"Kate, please." Daren halts in the street and faces her. "Do not do this to yourself. Rose is dead. No amount of hoping brings back the dead."

"How can you be certain?" Desperation strains her voice. "You heard what that thing said before it flew away. You all heard it! She told us to watch over Kevin and Suzie. Why would it say that if Rose weren't still in there, fighting for control?"

"Revenants awaken with the host's memories intact," Illuna says, Flower's eyes turning brilliant blue. "The spirit inherits everything the host knew. It is common for them to experience confusion at first, struggling to separate their own will from the impressions left in the flesh."

"Then there is still a chance—" Kate presses, but Illuna cuts her off cleanly.

"Even when a revenant honors the host's wishes, it remains an entirely separate entity," Illuna says. "A revenant cannot take root while the soul clings to the vessel. The mere existence of that creature is proof that Rose had already passed before Ulruk's servant claimed her flesh."

"But..." Kate's voice falters, her hands clenching into fists at her sides. "If we just..."

The words die in her throat. She looks down at the flagstones, her shoulders rigid, and says nothing more.

"I am sorry," Daren says softly, turning back toward the road.

We fall into step behind him. Kate lingers a moment before following, her eyes glued to the pavement. The remainder of the march passes in dead silence.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Monsters, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Monsters)


ID: B2-Ch01a-Pass-dead
TEXT:

