ID: B2-Ch01a-Sure-alive
TEXT:

"Sure, why not?" I say, taking the chain from Hadrik.

I twirl the amulet around my fingers. Arraka's muffled screeching rises in volume, but through the sealed casing the words blur into an unintelligible rasp. I am definitely better off not knowing what she is promising to do to my intestines.

"So, what do you think of our first trial?" Flower asks, skipping ahead to match Rose's pace.

"I think the idiot who dreamed it up can take his pinecones and shove them straight up his—"

"We heard you the first time, Hadrik," Daren interrupts. "The rules are set. Plenty of mages will lodge complaints about the absurdity of the task, but I am simply grateful we were not ordered to slaughter one another in the streets. That would have turned the city into a graveyard."

"But how will you track them down?" Flower asks. "I have lived in Varathia for years and never laid eyes on one."

"It's not as if you spent those years foraging for pinecones," I point out. "There must be someone in town who knows where they grow."

"I am not so certain," Rose says, glancing over her shoulder. "Herbology is my trade, yet glowing pinecones have never appeared in any text I have studied. They may be a very recent discovery."

"So the organizers haven't the faintest idea where to find them either," Hadrik says, scowling. "They're using the tournament as a free workforce to do their chores."

"I would not put it quite so bluntly, but—"

"I swear, the moment I get near that king of Thilias, I'm knocking him across the room," Hadrik grunts, cracking his knuckles. "Guards or no guards."

"You will do no such thing," Kate says coldly. "You are still forbidden from harming the locals."

"Damn it all, you're right," Hadrik mutters. He halts in his tracks, looking up at the sky. "Though maybe it isn't too late. Maybe Eiden will hand over the power if I ask nicely."

The dwarf plants his feet in the center of the lane and bellows at the rooftops.

"Eiden! Hey, Eiden! Do you hear me?! I want the power too! Stop skulking in the shadows and show yourself!"

"Hadrik, please!" Rose gives an anxious laugh, glancing at the shuttered windows lining the alley. "People live here. Keep your voice down. And keep moving, or you will lose sight of us in these turnings."

"Right, right," Hadrik mumbles, jogging to catch up. "Coming!"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch01a-Lover, v_current_scene = B2-Ch01a-Lover)


