ID: B2-Ch01a-Monsters
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch1_volunteer == 0) {
As we near the gates of the estate, Rose's younger brother and sister spot us from the courtyard and sprint down the gravel path to meet us.

"Where's Rose?" Suzie asks, craning her neck to peer behind our shoulders. "Did she stay behind at the clinic?"

We trade uneasy glances. Daren steps forward, his heavy pauldrons shifting as he rests a gentle palm on the girl's shoulder.

"Suzie," he says, his voice thick. "There is something I must tell you about your sister."

"Oh gods," Suzie whispers, her small face draining of color. "Is she..." She swallows hard. "Is she dead?"

The bluntness catches Daren off guard, but he does not evade her gaze.

"Yes," he says softly. "I am sorry. The fault is mine. I swore I would keep her safe, and I—"

"It's all right," Suzie says, forcing a tremulous smile. "Rose told us to be ready for this. She taught us how to cook, how to keep the house clean, how to manage everything on our own in case she never returned from one of her journeys."

Beside her, Kevin bites his lower lip, tears welling in the corners of his eyes.

"We promised her we wouldn't cry," Suzie says, her fingers clutching the fabric of her skirt. "We promised we would stay strong, and..." She drags a sleeve across her face. "And that we would remember her with a smile. That we would live our lives and be happy, and... and..."

The composure shatters all at once. Suzie buries her face in her hands, her shoulders heaving with ragged sobs. Kevin loses his grip as well, howling into the crook of his elbow.

"Now, now," a deep voice calls from the courtyard behind them. "What manner of monsters brings tears to such a lovely girl?"

A man strides down the gravel path toward us. He stands nearly as tall as Daren, broad-chested and lean, his linen shirt unlaced halfway down his chest. Thick dark hair falls to his shoulders, and a dense, bristling moustache frames his mouth. At his left hip hangs a gilded scabbard encrusted with rows of cut gems along the hilt. He drops to one knee beside Suzie and brushes the tears from her cheek with a calloused thumb.

"Did these ruffians trouble you, my dear Suzie?" he asks gently.

}
#if(v_b2_ch1_volunteer == 1) {
As we near the gates of the estate, Rose's younger brother and sister spot us from the courtyard and sprint down the gravel path to meet us.

"Where's Rose?" Suzie asks, craning her neck to peer behind our shoulders. "Did she stay behind at the clinic?"

The others look to me. I step forward and clear my throat, the words sticking in my chest.

"What is it?" Suzie's brow furrows as she reads my face. "Did something happen to Rose?"

"Yes," I say. "We were ambushed on the road to the clinic. We thought Rose was out of harm's way, but..."

I hesitate, searching for phrasing that will soften the blow.

"Oh gods," Suzie whispers, her small face draining of color. "Is she..." She swallows hard. "Is she dead?"

The direct question leaves me speechless. Before I can find my voice, Daren steps past me and drops to one knee in front of her, his head bowed.

"I am sorry," he says softly. "The fault is mine. I swore I would keep her safe, and I—"

